<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
{% include "head.liquid" %}
<body>
  {% include "header.liquid" %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Same opt-in as default.liquid: `wide: true` under `data:` in front matter.
    /archive/ uses this layout and wants the wide measure; a future prose page
    on this same layout (an About page, say) sets nothing and stays at the
    reading measure. Test it, never interpolate it — see default.liquid.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <main class="content-section">
    <div class="content-inner{% if page.data.wide %} content-inner--wide{% endif %}">
      {%- comment -%}
        Standalone pages render their own <h1> from front matter so the body
        markdown can start at whatever level it likes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% if page.title %}<h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>{% endif %}
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </main>

  {% include "footer.liquid" %}
</body>
</html>
